## Summary
The article reports that the non-performing ratio for the Big Four Financial Real Estate Trust Companies has reached 80%, indicating severe financial distress. This high default rate is directly linked to problems in real estate project finance (PF). It highlights potential systemic risks and instability in the real estate financing sector.

## Key Points
- Non-performing ratio for Big Four Financial Real Estate Trust Companies is at 80%.
- Defaults in real estate project finance (PF) are a major contributing factor.
- The situation suggests significant financial instability in the real estate sector.
- Impact may extend to broader financial systems due to interconnected risks.


